 lined up in tens`,friend:`frog`,known:!0,rungs:[W(1,`about 10, with ten lined up on a mat beside the bowl`),W(1,`about 20, with a loose heap of ten beside the bowl`),W(1,`about 20, with nothing to compare with`),W(2,`about 30`),W(2,`about 40`),W(2,`about 50`),W(3,`about 30 to 50, and which ten the heap is nearest to (47 is nearer 50)`),W(3,`big heaps by tens: about 60 or 70, with a heap of ten to measure with`),W(3,`about 100: ten mats of ten`,!1),W(3,`a scoop holds about 25: how many scoops for 100?`,!1),W(4,`the nearest hundred`,!1)]},{id:`balance`,subject:`maths`,name:`The same on both sides: making the scale level`,friend:`bunny`,known:!0,rungs:[W(1,`make it level: spoon sugar on until it matches the flour (up to 6)`),W(1,`how many more: some sugar is on already (within 10)`),W(1,`too much sugar: take spoons off until it is level (within 10)`),W(1,`is it level? one bag the same as two (4 + 3 and 7)`),W(2,`two bags make it: 8 + 6 balances 10 + 4 (within 20)`),W(2,`two jars the same: which pair balances 10? (halves and doubles)`),W(2,`tens and ones: bags of ten, then spoons (two digits to 49)`),W(3,`bags by their number: 3 bags of 4 balance 12 (equal groups)`),W(3,`a mystery jar: a jar and 5 balance 12, how many in the jar?`,!1),W(3,`which side is heavier, without counting (27 + 15 and 27 + 16)`,!1),W(4,`two weighings: two kinds of jar, found one after the other`,!1)]},{id:`spell-word`,subject:`writing`,name:`Spelling a word by its sounds`,friend:`kitty`,rungs:[W(1,`short vowels, one letter for each sound (milk, salt, bun)`),W(1,`two letters, one sound: ch, sh and doubles (egg, cherry, shells)`),W(1,`long vowels: a vowel team or a quiet e (cheese, cream)`),W(2,`r-vowels and -le (pepper, custard, sprinkles)`),W(2,`c before e says s (rice)`),W(2,`endings for more than one: -s, -ies (cherries, eggs, buns)`),W(3,`sound-alikes: the meaning picks the spelling (flour, sugar)`,!1),W(3,`long words, one beat at a time (spaghetti, pepperoni)`,!1)]},{id:`swap-letter`,subject